y":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"#### What language are you using?\r\n\r\nPython\r\n\r\n#### Have you tried latest version of polars?\r\n\r\nYes\r\n\r\n#### What version of polars are you using?\r\n\r\n0.13.31\r\n\r\n#### What operating system are you using polars on?\r\n\r\nWindows 10 x64\r\n\r\n#### What language version are you using\r\n\r\nPython 3.8\r\n\r\n#### Describe your bug.\r\n\r\nIf `DataFrame.pivot()` is called with an empty list of index columns, there is a memory allocation error.\r\n\r\nIn my application the list of index columns is not known in advance, and may or may not be empty.\r\n\r\n#### What are the steps to reproduce the behavior?\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport polars as pl\r\ndf = pl.DataFrame({'a': ['one', 'two', 'one', 'two'], 'b': [1, 2, 3, 4]})\r\ndf.pivot(columns='a', values='b', index=[], aggregate_fn='mean')\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### What is the actual behavior?\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndf.pivot(columns='a', values='b', index=[], aggregate_fn='mean')\r\n\r\nmemory allocation of 17179869184 bytes failed\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### What is the expected behavior?\r\n\r\nI would expect the call to succeed, grouping the original rows only by the columns specified in the \"columns\" argument. The result would be the same as the below:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndf.with_column(pl.lit(0).alias('dummy')).pivot(columns='a', values='b', index='dummy', aggregate_fn='mean').drop('dummy')\r\n\r\n┌─────┬─────┐\r\n│ one ┆ two │\r\n│ --- ┆ --- │\r\n│ f64 ┆ f64 │\r\n╞═════╪═════╡\r\n│ 2.0 ┆ 3.0 │\r\n└─────┴─────┘\r\n```\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"ritchie46","id":3023000,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMjMwMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3023000?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ritchie46","html_url":"https://github.com/ritchie46","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ritchie46/followers","following_url":"https